    "sections": {
        "description": "<h3>GDPR</h3>\n<p>According to the GDPR, the user must actively agree if content is to be loaded from third-party servers.<br />\nThe WordPress plugins <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/leaflet-map/\" rel=\"ugc\">Leaflet Map</a> and <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/extensions-leaflet-map/\" rel=\"ugc\">Extensions for Leaflet Map</a> are loading content from the defined tile servers as well as unpkg.com.<br />\nThis plugin requests the user&#8217;s permission to load the maps.<br />\nYou can customize the text and use it on your own responsibility.</p>\n<p>The plugin supports <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/theme-translation-for-polylang/\" rel=\"ugc\">Theme and plugin translation for Polylang (TTfP)</a>.</p>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<p>Documentation in <a href=\"https://leafext.de/doku/dsgvo/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">German</a>, <a href=\"https://leafext.de/en/doku/dsgvo/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">English</a> and an <a href=\"https://leafext.de/extra/dsgvo-example/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">example</a>.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ul>\n<li>Install and configure the plugin <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/leaflet-map/\" rel=\"ugc\">Leaflet Map</a>.</li>\n<li>Install and configure the plugin <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/extensions-leaflet-map/\" rel=\"ugc\">Extensions for Leaflet Map</a>.</li>\n<li>Then install this plugin.</li>\n<li>Go to Settings &#8211; Leaflet Map &#8211; Leaflet Map GDPR and get documentation and settings options.</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"is%20that%20enough%20to%20comply%20with%20the%20gdpr%3F\">\nIs that enough to comply with the GDPR?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<ul>\n<li>I don&#8217;t know, ask a law expert.</li>\n</ul>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h3>3.2</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>WordPress 6.9.1 enqueue warning fixed</li>\n<li>admin&#8217;s special condition removed</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Previous</h3>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/hupe13/extensions-leaflet-map-dsgvo/blob/main/changes.md\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">Changelog</a></p>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Respect the DSGVO / GDPR when you use Leaflet Map and Extensions for Leaflet Map.",
    "description": "<h3>GDPR</h3>\n<p>According to the GDPR, the user must actively agree if content is to be loaded from third-party servers.<br />\nThe WordPress plugins <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/leaflet-map/\" rel=\"ugc\">Leaflet Map</a> and <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/extensions-leaflet-map/\" rel=\"ugc\">Extensions for Leaflet Map</a> are loading content from the defined tile servers as well as unpkg.com.<br />\nThis plugin requests the user&#8217;s permission to load the maps.<br />\nYou can customize the text and use it on your own responsibility.</p>\n<p>The plugin supports <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/plugins/theme-translation-for-polylang/\" rel=\"ugc\">Theme and plugin translation for Polylang (TTfP)</a>.</p>\n<h3>Documentation</h3>\n<p>Documentation in <a href=\"https://leafext.de/doku/dsgvo/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">German</a>, <a href=\"https://leafext.de/en/doku/dsgvo/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">English</a> and an <a href=\"https://leafext.de/extra/dsgvo-example/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">example</a>.</p>\n",
